  "compositionNotes": {
    "objects": "Objects are the nouns. Most systems center on a small cluster of Objects plus supporting ones.",
    "properties": "Properties are attached to Objects. Many are generic (Status, Owner, CreatedAt) and should be reused.",
    "actions": "Actions operate on Objects or collections of Objects. Prefer declarative descriptions that agents can map to API or UI handlers.",
    "interfaces": "Interfaces render Objects and accept Actions. A single Object often has multiple Interfaces (Table + Detail + Form).",
    "intelligence": "Intelligence atoms wrap model calls. They should be treated as side-effecting services with clear contracts.",
    "rules": "Rules bind Triggers/Conditions to Actions and are the primary mechanism for automation and governance."
  }
